Acute respiratory failure is a state of disturbed gas exchange that shows up as abnormal arterial blood gas values while the person breathes room air (21% oxygen):
- arterial oxygen tension (PaO2) below 60 mmHg, which is the hypoxemia;
- arterial carbon dioxide tension (PaCO2) above 50 mmHg;
- pH below 7.30.

It comes in three categories: hypoxic failure, hypercapnic ventilatory failure, or a combination of both.
